<title>FRANCE: Algerian steel company makes 77.9 mln dinars profit.</title>
<headline>Algerian steel company makes 77.9 mln dinars profit.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria's iron and steel products maker, COPROSID, made a profit of 77.9 million dinars ($1.4 million) in 1995, the official Algerian news agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said the company, National Enterprise for Iron and Steel Products and Coproducts, which is based in the northeastern town of Annaba, would use the profit to pay dividends and to increase reserves and capital.</p>
<p>Current capital is 50 million dinars, said APS which gave no other details.</p>
<p>($1 = 55 dinars)</p>
</text>
